Blackdrift: flat ground behind the home screen instead of Focus's gradient.

Why: UrlInputFragment paints R.drawable.home_background, which Focus ships as
vectors with literal lavender (light) and purple (dark) gradient stops in
drawable, drawable-night, drawable-land and drawable-land-night. A colour
mapping (patch 0208) cannot reach literal stops, and DESIGN.md says the home
gradient goes flat to the ground. Same-name drawables in the focus flavor
source set replace each qualifier (a more specific main/res variant would
otherwise win at night or in landscape). Each is a rectangle filled with the
theme-aware @color/blackdrift_ground from patch 0202. Verbatim copies of
blackdrift/branding/android/focus/res, generated by build.mjs.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

diff --git a/app/src/focus/res/drawable-land-night/home_background.xml b/app/src/focus/res/drawable-land-night/home_background.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0b449d3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/app/src/focus/res/drawable-land-night/home_background.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- Home screen background: flat ground (DESIGN.md → Colour), replaces Focus's gradient. Generated by blackdrift/branding/scripts/build.mjs. Do not edit by hand. -->
+<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
+    android:shape="rectangle">
+    <solid android:color="@color/blackdrift_ground"/>
+</shape>
